hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27905","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, he said: I heard Jabir, he said: Umm Mubashshir, the wife of Zayd ibn Harithah, narrated to me, she said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in a garden, and he said: Is this yours. I said: Yes. He said: Who planted it, a Muslim or a disbeliever. I said: A Muslim. He said: There is no Muslim who sows or plants a planting, and a bird or a human or a beast or anything eats from it, except it is charity for him. My father said: And 'I heard Jabir' was not in the copy, and Ibn Numayr said: I heard Amir."
"27906","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed me, he said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir, he said: Umm Mubashshir narrated to me that she heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with Hafsah saying: None of the companions of the tree, those who pledged beneath it, shall enter the Fire, if Allah wills. She said: Yes indeed, O Messenger of Allah. So he rebuked her. Then Hafsah said: And there is none of you but shall come to it. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has said: Then We shall save those who feared Allah and leave the wrongdoers therein on their knees."
